    <dcterms:title>The Rover</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rover_(novel)</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Produced by Chuck Greif and the Online Distributed
Proofreading Team at http://www.pgdp.net (This file was
produced from images available at The Internet Archive)</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"The Rover" by Joseph Conrad is a novel written between 1921 and 1922. Set in southern France during the French Revolution and Napoleon's rise, it follows Peyrol, a master-gunner and pirate who has spent fifty years roaming distant seas. Seeking refuge at an isolated farmhouse, he encounters outcasts and becomes entangled in their struggles. The story explores his attempt to escape a violent past and his search for identity and allegiance, culminating in one final voyage. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 80.1 (6th grade). Easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
